# Scanner exceptions

Do not add `mobsf-ignore`, `nosemgrep`, CodeQL suppressions, OSV ignore lists, or extra
`paths-ignore` / `--exclude` entries to make a check pass.

1. Fix the code (example: Room `AutoMigration` instead of annotated `execSQL`).
2. If the skip is **scope** (analog pins, `build/`, test classpaths, generated protobuf), add a row to
   [`docs/scanner-exceptions.md`](../../docs/scanner-exceptions.md) explaining why this is
   not a product finding and why a code change is the wrong tool.
3. Finding-level ignores are allowed only with a table row: rule id, location, why the
   code cannot be the fix, and a review date.

Guardrails-compliance already forbids silent suppressions. This file is the consuming-repo
place those scanner skips must be listed.
